35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The findings suggest a divide between tangible and digital assets. I've noticed that hardware-based holdings require external appraisals, which adds significant time and cost to our closing process. We must consider how a new holding affects our reporting efficiency.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data shows a clear pattern. Our successful exits were quiet, back-office tools, while the write-off involved physical premises and labor. This suggests our returns come from low-overhead software, not the operational narratives we often highlight.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings are concerning. Follow-on calls are occurring twice as fast as modeled, and our credit line only provides liquidity against physical stock, leaving our subscription-based assets useless as security. We are burning through cash far too quickly.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Hmm, that's a bit worrying! I found out that while we can find support staff quickly, getting supervisors or field crews takes forever. Plus, our software partners are totally swamped with board seats!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The data confirms my suspicions. Security reviews for sensitive data take three times longer than expected, and hardware dependencies create unpredictable delays. We must be wary of any candidate whose deployment depends on external approvals or physical supply chains.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is clear we are all seeing fragments of a larger struggle. If we choose a company with physical assets, we risk further complicating our reporting and adding to the burden of our quarter-end.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Exactly. The retention data also shows that the shopkeeper tool—which likely has more physical interaction—struggled with price rises. We should prioritize a lean, software-driven model that doesn't rely on the operational complexities that led to our write-off.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"I agree. Given that our reserves are depleting faster than planned and our credit line is restrictive, we cannot afford a capital-intensive investment. We must prioritize a candidate with minimal follow-on requirements and high liquidity.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Wait, if we pick something that needs a lot of field crews or supervisors, we're going to be stuck searching for months! And our software partners can't possibly take on any more board seats right now!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"The common thread here is friction. Whether it is security reviews, supply chains, or staffing, external dependencies are our primary risk. We should avoid any candidate that requires physical deployment or high-level regulatory clearance.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We are all describing a need for simplicity. To preserve our peace of mind and the integrity of our reporting, we should seek a candidate that offers a clean, digital path without the weight of physical appraisals.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"Simplicity is not just about peace of mind; it is about survival. We must avoid the trap of investing in ""exciting"" operational stories that actually hide high overhead and fragile customer loyalty. Lean software is our only proven win.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"I agree. We are in a precarious financial position. We need a candidate that requires very little upfront capital and has a low probability of unexpected follow-on calls. A lean, digital model is the only safe choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm totally on board with the lean software idea! If we pick something digital, we won't have to stress about those long hiring times for field crews, and our partners can actually breathe!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,It seems we have reached a consensus. We must prioritize a candidate with a streamlined deployment process and no physical dependencies. Any friction in the initial rollout is a risk we cannot afford.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see us align so naturally. By choosing a path of simplicity and digital agility, we protect not only our capital but also our collective well-being. I am ready to see the candidates.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I am also ready. Let us ensure we apply these criteria strictly. We must not let a compelling pitch distract us from the fact that lean, digital tools are what actually deliver our returns.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I am ready as well. We must remain disciplined. The financial data is clear: we cannot risk another capital-heavy venture. I will vote for the candidate that presents the lowest risk to our liquidity.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm ready too! Let's find a company that's super lean and doesn't need a million new people right away. I can't wait to see who the candidates are!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am ready. We have identified the critical failure points. I will be looking for the candidate with the fewest external dependencies and the most predictable path to deployment.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
